From bc782a9d9745604b11cd9dca59a4f20ab014bbdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:57:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: request 320x240 instead of 640x480

Independent peer review (session "dossage-24", operator-requested perf
audit, arrived mid-implementation of patch 0018) found a structural gap
against doskutsu (a sibling DOS port on this hub that hits 17.8-18.6fps
on the same 486DX2-50): doskutsu locks 320x240 fullscreen; dossage has
been running 640x480. At 320x240, blowUpFactor drops from 6 to 3
(maxBlowUpFactor = screenWidth / width, game.cpp), so the blown-up
sub-rect shrinks roughly 4x in pixel count through every stage of the
flip path (blowup/native-write, and present) -- no fidelity loss, since
gameImage stays 100x12 native regardless of display resolution; the
game just gets shown with less upscaling.

Two changes:

1. `settings/width.ini` 640 -> 320, `settings/height.ini` 480 -> 240.
   Read via SettingsManager at startup (game.cpp ~700-716) and override
   the hard-coded screenWidth/screenHeight defaults -- a data-file
   change, not a code change, so there's no game logic to get wrong
   here.

2. `SDL_SetHint( SDL_HINT_DOS_PIN_WINDOW_TO_NATIVE_MODE, "1" )` before
   SDL_Init (game.cpp), alongside the existing
   SDL_HINT_DOS_ALLOW_DIRECT_FRAMEBUFFER hint. Per that hint's own doc
   comment (SDL_hints.h): SDL3's window/fullscreen reconciliation can
   fire a second, later mode-set call to the display's hard-coded
   "desktop mode" (640x480 on this backend) after the app's own
   requested-dimensions mode-set already succeeded, silently discarding
   the smaller mode the app actually asked for -- doskutsu needed this
   exact hint for the same 320x240-on-this-hub's-backend scenario. Set
   unconditionally since it's documented as a no-op when the app-
   requested mode was never honored in the first place.

**Real uncertainty, not glossed over**: that same hint's doc comment
explicitly calls out this port's actual test rig's card -- "ATI Mach64
+ M64VBE... doesn't expose any 320x240 modes because the Mach64-CT chip
lacks line-doubling circuitry" -- as a case where the app-requested
mode may never be honored at all, silently falling back to 640x480
regardless of this patch. UniVBE (the software VESA extender this rig
actually boots through, confirmed via this repo's own earlier
`oem_string='Universal VESA VBE 6.70'` finding) might still synthesize
320x240 via software scan-doubling even if the card ROM alone can't --
but that's a real question needing real-hardware confirmation, not an
assumption either way.

Verified under DOSBox-X (S3 Trio64 emulation): `SDLDBG.LOG` confirms
`mode-set #1 (entry): requested id=0x0190 320x240 32bpp` succeeded,
`vram_w=320 vram_h=240 fb_size=307200` -- this emulated card DOES have
a 320x240 mode (unlike what's documented for the real Mach64), so this
test confirms the settings-read/hint mechanism works correctly but
can't confirm whether the real rig's mode negotiation succeeds the same
way. Game rendered correctly at the new resolution (screenshot
comparison unaffected by DOSBox-X's own window-scaling display
behavior, which is unrelated to the actual internal VESA mode).
FLIPDBG.LOG shows the native-format fast path (patch 0018) stayed
active at the new resolution too. Clean boot/play/ESCAPE-quit, no hang.

Real-hardware confirmation is the essential next step -- specifically,
whether `SDLDBG.LOG`'s own mode-set line and the printed "Screen
dimensions for fullscreen mode" line actually show 320x240 taking
effect on the real Mach64+UniVBE rig, or whether it silently stays at
640x480 (which would mean this specific fix is a no-op on this
hardware, useful to know either way, and would still leave patch
0018's own real win intact regardless).
---
 gameSource/game.cpp            | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 gameSource/settings/height.ini |  2 +-
 gameSource/settings/width.ini  |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gameSource/game.cpp b/gameSource/game.cpp
index 71c6918..a51f471 100644
--- a/gameSource/game.cpp
+++ b/gameSource/game.cpp
@@ -666,6 +666,28 @@ int mainFunction( int inArgCount, char **inArgs ) {
     // <SDL3/SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h>'s "When to use this" section).
     // Must be set before SDL_Init.
     SDL_SetHint( SDL_HINT_DOS_ALLOW_DIRECT_FRAMEBUFFER, "1" );
+
+    // DOS-PORT: this port now requests 320x240 (settings/width.ini,
+    // settings/height.ini -- see the maxBlowUpFactor comment below) to
+    // cut per-frame pixel counts through the whole flip path roughly 4x
+    // versus the previous 640x480 default, following the same pattern
+    // doskutsu already uses successfully on this hub's shared backend.
+    // SDL3's window/fullscreen reconciliation can fire a SECOND, later
+    // mode-set call to the display's hard-coded "desktop mode" (640x480
+    // on this backend) after the app's own requested-dimensions mode-set
+    // already succeeded -- without this hint, that second call can win,
+    // silently discarding the smaller mode the app actually asked for
+    // (see SDL_HINT_DOS_PIN_WINDOW_TO_NATIVE_MODE's own doc comment for
+    // the full mechanism and a from-life example of the resulting bug:
+    // "game renders only in a small box in the corner of the screen").
+    // Explicitly harmless if the app-requested mode was never honored in
+    // the first place -- e.g. this specific rig's ATI Mach64 chip is
+    // separately documented as exposing no native 320x240 VBE mode at
+    // all (no line-doubling circuitry), so this hint alone does not
+    // guarantee 320x240 actually takes effect here; only real-hardware
+    // confirmation of the boot log's negotiated mode does. Set
+    // regardless since it's a no-op when not needed.
+    SDL_SetHint( SDL_HINT_DOS_PIN_WINDOW_TO_NATIVE_MODE, "1" );
 #endif
 
     // DOS-PORT: SDL3 removed SDL_INIT_NOPARACHUTE (no signal-handler
diff --git a/gameSource/settings/height.ini b/gameSource/settings/height.ini
index 7ad8022..eaea6f5 100644
--- a/gameSource/settings/height.ini
+++ b/gameSource/settings/height.ini
@@ -1 +1 @@
-480
\ No newline at end of file
+240
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/gameSource/settings/width.ini b/gameSource/settings/width.ini
index c328260..194ba8c 100644
--- a/gameSource/settings/width.ini
+++ b/gameSource/settings/width.ini
@@ -1 +1 @@
-640
\ No newline at end of file
+320
\ No newline at end of file
-- 
